Venetium 0060 - no automatic stack-variable initialization in the DSP-only codec targets.
From the performance research (C:\handoff\PERF-RESEARCH.md, item S2), his "fix all".
Chromium initializes every stack variable (pattern in non-official builds, zero in official ones). DSP kernels keep
fixed-size scratch arrays they overwrite in full, so the fill is a pure memset per block: jsimd_idct_islow_neon (the
JPEG IDCT Blink uses) called memset(0xFF, 64) twice per 8x8 block before its first load; dav1d's cdef and loop
restoration likewise per block. libaom ("13% slowdown") and V8 already opt out the same way. Applied with
configs -= [ "//build/config/compiler:default_init_stack_vars" ] to the DSP-only targets: libjpeg_turbo "simd";
dav1d "dav1d_8bit", "dav1d_10bit", "dav1d_arm", "dav1d_x86"; libvpx's intrinsics source sets (NEON, MMX..AVX-512);
libwebp "libwebp_dsp" and its NEON/SSE2/SSE4.1/AVX2 variants. Bitstream parsers (libjpeg core, dav1d's decoder,
ffmpeg, which keeps its parsers in the same target) keep the initialization. Small hardening trade in sandboxed codec
code that only fills and reads its own scratch buffers.

